    {
      "id": "AGUI-DC-006",
      "page": "en/03-gui-system/08-dialogs-modals.md",
      "disposition": "accept exact repair",
      "old_text": "Because Enforce Script has no closures or delegates, routing the result back by function name -- the target object plus a method name string -- is the standard way to give a reusable dialog a callback. Any admin-tool style dialog box that needs to hand a result back to an arbitrary caller uses this same name-based routing.",
      "final_new_text": "This example routes results by target object and method name. DayZ also exposes `func` callbacks and `ScriptInvoker`; choose the callback mechanism supported by the API you are using and keep callback targets alive until the dialog finishes.",
      "reason": "Pinned VideoWidget callback and ScriptInvoker APIs refute the universal name-string claim without asserting closures.",
      "council_json": "council-early.json",
      "council_report": "council-early-REPORT.md",
      "editorial_outcome": "accepted"
    },
    {
      "id": "AGUI-DC-007",
      "page": "en/03-gui-system/07-styles-fonts.md",
      "disposition": "reject",
      "old_text": "| Imageset XML and native formats are equivalent | Both define sprite regions | The native brace format is what the engine processes fastest. XML format works but adds a parsing step; use native format for production |",
      "final_new_text": null,
      "reason": "LoadWidgetImageSet declaration proves neither accepted formats nor parser performance; proposed replacement remains speculative.",
      "council_json": "council-early.json",
      "council_report": "council-early-REPORT.md",
      "editorial_outcome": "rejected"
    },
    {
      "id": "AGUI-DC-008",
      "page": "en/04-file-formats/06-pbo-packing.md",
      "disposition": "accept exact repair",
      "old_text": "2. **Always set a prefix.** Without a prefix, the engine cannot resolve paths to your mod's content. Every PBO must have a correct `-prefix`.",
      "final_new_text": "2. **Verify the PBO prefix.** Set `-prefix` explicitly when you need a specific virtual path; otherwise Addon Builder may calculate it automatically. In either case, confirm the stored prefix matches all resource references.",
      "reason": "Official Addon Builder revision 341605 says an absent prefix is calculated automatically.",
      "council_json": "council-early.json",
      "council_report": "council-early-REPORT.md",
      "editorial_outcome": "accepted"
    },
    {
